WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.232
Google Cloud CLI security is a repeatable
engineering practice.

2
00:00:05.312 --> 00:00:07.550
Start with target validation.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:13.136
Confirm project, account, active
configuration, region, zone, identity,

4
00:00:13.216 --> 00:00:17.260
environment label, and resource target
before action.

5
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.073
Do not rely on accidental active settings,
inherited variables,

6
00:00:22.153 --> 00:00:26.713
stale configurations, or defaults that
have not been checked.

7
00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.718
Use scoped IAM and protect credentials.

8
00:00:29.798 --> 00:00:35.305
Match permissions to the script's actual
job, separate read-only, deploy,

9
00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:41.064
rollback, and owner-level access, and
prefer Workload Identity Federation,

10
00:00:41.144 --> 00:00:46.909
service account impersonation, or managed
runtime identity where practical.

11
00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:51.377
Protect login sessions, Application
Default Credentials,

12
00:00:51.457 --> 00:00:56.878
service account key material, CI/CD
secrets, and environment variables.

13
00:00:56.958 --> 00:01:00.228
Rotate, revoke, and review access over
time.

14
00:01:00.308 --> 00:01:05.470
Invoke the Google Cloud CLI from Bash with
fixed, reviewable patterns.

15
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:11.229
Quote values, use arrays where useful,
validate command groups, operations,

16
00:01:11.309 --> 00:01:17.418
project IDs, regions, zones, resources,
paths, filters, and output destinations,

17
00:01:17.498 --> 00:01:20.854
and check exit status before trusting
output.

18
00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:25.924
Parse JSON deliberately and write files
only to approved locations.

19
00:01:26.004 --> 00:01:31.167
Finally, guard high-impact actions with
organization policy checks,

20
00:01:31.247 --> 00:01:36.754
previews, validation, approvals, and
rollback planning where available.

21
00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:41.910
Treat deletion, overwrite, public
exposure, permission expansion,

22
00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:44.916
and encryption changes with extra care.

23
00:01:44.996 --> 00:01:48.524
Log safely, monitor audit and identity
records,

24
00:01:48.604 --> 00:01:53.422
respond quickly to credential exposure or
wrong-target changes,

25
00:01:53.502 --> 00:01:57.460
and improve scripts and roles through
regular review.
